+
+# case_insensitive_autoescape
+
+## Why
+Flask's default Jinja autoescape selector fails to recognize supported template
+extensions when their filename uses uppercase or mixed case.
+
+## What
+- Normalize the filename's case before checking the existing supported
+  extensions.
+- Add regression coverage for mixed-case supported extensions and preserve the
+  unsupported and no-filename paths.
+
+## Acceptance
+- [x] Mixed-case `.html`, `.htm`, `.xml`, `.xhtml`, and `.svg` filenames enable
+  autoescaping — check: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_templating.py -q`
+- [x] Unsupported filenames return false and `None` returns true — check:
+  `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_templating.py -q`
+
+## Impact
+`Flask.create_jinja_environment` installs this selector as Jinja's default
+autoescape callback. The change only normalizes the filename for matching, so
+supported lowercase names retain their result and unsupported names remain
+unsupported.
