+### Root cause: implicit-assumption
+
+The default Jinja autoescape selector compared filename suffixes case
+sensitively, implicitly assuming template extension casing was lowercase.
+Fix: normalize the filename before testing the existing supported suffixes.
+Prevention: regression tests cover each supported extension with mixed case.
+
+### Verify: Default Jinja autoescape recognizes supported extensions regardless of filename case
